From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MC-xiaonan <2106104879@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:22:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 2: 15 Leaves-inspired fixes and micro-optimisations

Original reimplementations of a shortlisted set of Leaves-style
patches, each gated behind a LcsXNMCConfig toggle with toggle-off
preserving exact vanilla behaviour:

- allocation/GC micro-optimisations (LivingEntity, AttributeMap,
  SecondaryPoiSensor, EntityBasedExplosionDamageCalculator,
  LocalMobCapCalculator, KineticWeapon, ItemUtils)
- redstone timing legacy-behaviour toggles (CopperBulbBlock,
  CrafterBlock)
- neutral-mob anger-target fix (NeutralMob)
- update-suppression crash-avoidance subsystem: new
  UpdateSuppressionException control-flow signal thrown from verified
  race-prone block/block-entity cast sites (ShelfBlock) and neighbor
  update dispatch (NeighborUpdater), caught at tick/packet dispatch
  loops (ServerLevel, Level, PacketProcessor) without letting a
  suppressed side effect discard an unrelated healthy entity
- update-suppression-sound: re-validate a sculk sensor's BlockState
  against the live world before activating, since vibrations can take
  several ticks to arrive (SculkSensorBlock)
- update-suppression-item-drop: guarantee level.captureDrops is always
  cleared and any already-captured drops are still spawned even if the
  destroy sequence throws partway through (ServerPlayerGameMode)
- update-suppression-block-place: revert a block placement instead of
  leaving the world and the player's item stack desynced if
  setPlacedBy throws a suppressed update exception (BlockItem)

